# Local environment and caches -- never committed from anywhere in this tree.
.venv/
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/

# ONLY THE DELIVERABLES ARE TRACKED, and the pattern is deny-then-allow for the same reason
# `component_c_rl/.gitignore` gives: a deny list has to be extended by hand every time a new
# directory appears, and the thing that gets forgotten is exactly the thing that should not be
# published.
#
# WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST AT ALL. The repository root's .gitignore ignores `*.md` wholesale and
# re-includes an allow-list of named files ("Markdown documentation is local-only except the three
# approved README files"). Without a nested .gitignore here, `README.md`, `BUILDLOG.md` and
# `DATASET_GUIDE.md` would all be silently untracked -- and `cognitive_dataset.csv` is not matched
# by any root allow-list either. `component_c_rl` solved this the same way, with its own nested
# file rather than by extending the root's allow-list; this follows that precedent.
/*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!BUILDLOG.md
!DATASET_GUIDE.md
!manifest.json
!cognitive_dataset.csv
!notebooks/
notebooks/*
!notebooks/README.md
!notebooks/*.ipynb
!notebooks/outputs/

# Model artefacts are NOT tracked. None exists today (see README, "What does not exist"); if B2
# ever produces one, publishing it is a separate decision with its own approval, not a side effect
# of dropping a file in this folder.
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.onnx
